om-pose assets: not under the OpenMarch application's license

The files in this folder (bodies/, clips/ and manifest.json) come from
OpenMarch's om-pose repository; SOURCE.json records the commit. They don't
ship under the app's license (ADR 0010 D-7, correction of 2026-10-11).

- The clips, derived from 2019 Cadets footage, are in the counsel gate: no
  release that ships them goes out before counsel answers lawyer Q3.
- The meshes (the reference bodies and the v4 skeleton) take CC0 1.0 once Q3
  is answered and om-pose adopts a license upstream.

See docs/adr/0010-3d-view.md (D-7 and D-21) and docs/3d/props-spec.md
section 10.
